  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "If Alan and Barry paint a house together, then they take 3 days. If Barry and Calvin paint a house together, then they take 4 days. If Calvin and Alan paint a house together, then they take 5 days. How long would it take to paint a house if all three worked together?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p18-q7-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{120}{47}\\text{ days}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p18-q7-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Add the work completed by the three pairs over a common time, then halve it because each painter is counted twice.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "In 60 days, Alan and Barry paint $60\\div3=20$ houses, Barry and Calvin paint $60\\div4=15$ houses, and Calvin and Alan paint $60\\div5=12$ houses. Adding the pairs counts each painter's work twice.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Houses painted by all three in 60 days}&=\\frac{20+15+12}{2}\\\\\\text{Houses painted by all three in 60 days}&=\\frac{47}{2}\\\\\\text{Time for one house}&=60\\div\\frac{47}{2}\\\\\\text{Time for one house}&=\\frac{120}{47}\\text{ days}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
